## 2. AWS Infrastructure

### Infrastructure map

```
<% if (modules.backend) { -%>
EC2:
  <%= projectName %>-staging  -> staging environment (branch: staging)
  <%= projectName %>-prod     -> production environment (branch: prod)

RDS:
  PostgreSQL         -> shared instance, separate DBs per environment
                       (<%= projectName %>_staging_db + <%= projectName %>_prod_db)

<% } -%>
<% if (modules.web) { -%>
S3:
  <%= projectName %>-site     -> web static hosting
<% } -%>
  <%= projectName %>-media    -> user-uploaded media files

CloudFront:
  -> Distribution in front of S3 (<% if (modules.web) { %>site + <% } %>media CDN)

SSM Parameter Store:
  -> Stores all secrets for both environments
  -> Used by EC2 instances to inject env vars at deploy time
```

### SSM Parameter naming convention

```
/<%= projectName %>/{environment}/{parameter_name}
Examples:
  /<%= projectName %>/staging/DATABASE_URL
  /<%= projectName %>/prod/DATABASE_URL
  /<%= projectName %>/staging/JWT_SECRET_KEY
  /<%= projectName %>/prod/JWT_SECRET_KEY
```

All parameters: SecureString type -- never String for secrets.

### S3 media uploads

- Bucket policy: private by default -- no public access
- CloudFront signed URLs or presigned S3 URLs for serving media
- Uploads go through backend API (never direct from client with hardcoded credentials)
- CORS configured for specific origins only
- Presigned URL expiry: max 1 hour for downloads, 15 min for uploads
- Flag every new bucket or policy change to the security agent

### Infrastructure as Code

- All resources defined in IaC -- never click-ops in production
- Use AWS CDK or Terraform -- follow whichever already exists in the project
- Environments are isolated: staging never accesses prod DB, prod never accesses staging

<% } else { %>
## 2. Infrastructure

### Environment isolation

- Staging and production environments are strictly isolated.
- Never allow staging to access production databases or resources.
- All secrets managed via environment variables or secrets manager — never hardcoded.

<% } %>

