### Release checklist -- every submission

#### Version management

<% if (mobileFramework === 'expo-rn-nativewind') { %>
- [ ] Bump `version` in `app.json` (semantic: MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH)
- [ ] Bump `ios.buildNumber` (integer, always increasing)
- [ ] Bump `android.versionCode` (integer, always increasing)
- [ ] Commit version bump before triggering<% if (mobileFramework === 'expo-rn-nativewind') { %> EAS<% } %> production build
<% } else if (mobileFramework === 'flutter') { %>
- [ ] Bump `version` in `pubspec.yaml` (format: MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH+buildNumber)
- [ ] Build number must always increase for both iOS and Android
- [ ] Commit version bump before triggering production build
<% } %>

#### Pre-submission

- [ ] Production build succeeded (check CI/CD pipeline)
- [ ] Tested on physical iOS device (not just simulator)
- [ ] Tested on physical Android device (not just emulator)
- [ ] Changelog written
- [ ] Screenshots current (if UI changed since last submission)

#### iOS -- App Store Connect

- [ ] Build uploaded<% if (mobileFramework === 'expo-rn-nativewind') { %> (EAS submits automatically with `eas submit`)<% } %>
- [ ] TestFlight internal testing: distribute to internal testers, minimum 1 day
- [ ] Privacy manifest present (`PrivacyInfo.xcprivacy`) -- required by Apple
- [ ] Privacy nutrition labels accurate (data collected, data linked to user)
- [ ] Age rating verified and matches app content
- [ ] App description localized
- [ ] Support URL and marketing URL filled
- [ ] Demo account provided (Apple reviewer needs login access)
- [ ] Submit for review

#### Android -- Google Play Console

- [ ] AAB uploaded to internal testing track
- [ ] Passed internal testing -> promote to production
- [ ] Target API level current (required: Android 14 / API 34+)
- [ ] Content rating questionnaire complete
- [ ] Store listing descriptions and screenshots complete
- [ ] Data safety section complete (matches actual data collection)
- [ ] Signing key: use Google Play App Signing (never manage keystore manually)

### Common rejection reasons

**Apple:**
- Camera/photo library permissions without usage description strings
- Push notification permission prompt without explanation
- Location usage without `NSLocationWhenInUseUsageDescription`
- Demo account not working during review

**Google:**
- Sensitive permissions (camera, storage) without clear rationale in store listing
- Data safety section not reflecting actual data collection (e.g., location)

<% if (mobileFramework === 'expo-rn-nativewind') { %>
### OTA update workflow (Expo Updates)

1. Check changes since last update
2. Confirm OTA-compatible (no native module changes -- native changes require full build)
3. Execute: `npm run update:staging` or `npm run update:production`
4. Report update status
<% } %>

### Post-launch monitoring (first 7 days)

- Check crash rate daily in App Store Connect + Google Play Console
- Monitor reviews -- respond to 1-star reviews within 24h
- Watch for rating drops that signal a bad build
- If crash rate > 1%: prepare hotfix immediately

<% } %>

