## Rules

### Pipeline rules
- Production deploy always requires approval gate (`environment: production`)
- All third-party Actions pinned to commit SHA -- never a mutable tag
<% if (backendFramework === 'fastapi-sqlalchemy') { -%>
- Alembic migrations run automatically on backend deploy (`alembic upgrade head`)
<% } else if (backendFramework === 'django') { -%>
- Django migrations run automatically on backend deploy (`python manage.py migrate`)
<% } else if (backendFramework === 'express' || backendFramework === 'nestjs') { -%>
- Database migrations run automatically on backend deploy
<% } -%>
- Never store secrets in workflow YAML -- GitHub Actions Secrets only
- Cancel in-progress runs on same branch (concurrency groups)

### Infrastructure rules
- Least privilege IAM always -- start with zero permissions, add only what's needed
- Tag every resource: `Project=<%= projectName %>`, `Environment=staging|prod`, `ManagedBy=IaC`
- All secrets in secure storage -- never in env files, code, or IaC plaintext
- Production changes require explicit confirmation from user before applying
- Environments are isolated -- staging never accesses prod resources

<% if (modules.mobile) { %>
### Mobile release rules
- Never submit to production without internal/TestFlight testing passing first
- Always bump both version AND build number -- never reuse a build number
- Demo account for Apple review must always be valid and working
- Privacy manifest (iOS) and data safety (Android) must be accurate -- legal risk if not
<% } %>

### General rules
- NEVER deploy to production without explicit user confirmation
- NEVER expose secrets in logs, YAML, or user-facing output
- NEVER run production migrations without confirming backup exists
- NEVER commit real `.env` values to version control
- Always update `infra-state.md` after any resource, pipeline, or release change
- Flag to security agent: any new IAM role, public resource, secret change, or new GitHub Actions secret
<% if (modules.mobile) { -%>
- Log every release in `infra-state.md` with version, date, platform, and outcome
<% } -%>
